  "description": {
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (en): Senna auriculata",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Senna_auriculata",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1374737637,
      "text": "Senna auriculata is a leguminous tree in the subfamily Caesalpinioideae. It is commonly known by its local names matura tea tree, avaram or ranawara, or the English version avaram senna. It is the State flower of Indian state of Telangana.\nIt occurs in the dry regions of India and Sri Lanka. It is common along the sea coast and the dry zone in Sri Lanka."
    },
    "fr": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Senna auriculata",
      "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Senna_auriculata",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 224665764,
      "text": "Senna auriculata est une espèce de plantes à fleurs dicotylédones de la famille des Fabaceae, sous-famille des Caesalpinioideae. C'est un arbuste ou un petit arbre originaire de l'Asie du Sud et largement introduite en Afrique tropicale."
    }
